Third-party components
----------------------

None from outside this project. Study has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on
25/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used to write the deck exports
- srs-kit 0.2.0 — docs/play/srs-kit.js — SM-2 spaced repetition. This is the scheduler: the app
  does not reimplement it, and tests assert that the kit is the thing doing the scheduling.

None of the three is modified. None makes a network request.

On OCR
------

The Codex prompt asks for on-device OCR of handwritten notes. There is no OCR component in
this estate, so Study does not ship one, does not claim one, and says so on the page: the notes
are pasted or typed. Everything downstream of the text — cards, gaps, the schedule, the tutor —
works exactly as specified.
